## ARTI-PATCH: expo-modules-core@2.2.3 — web module registration

### Why this patch exists

`registerWebModule` in `expo-modules-core@2.2.3` reads the module name from
`moduleImplementation.name`. When the web bundle is minified (production
build), class names are mangled to short identifiers (`e`, `t`, etc.) — so
two unrelated modules end up registering under the same name and the
second one silently replaces the first.

### What the patch changes

1. Accept an optional explicit `name?: string` argument so the caller can
   pass a stable identifier instead of relying on `.name`.
2. Fall back to `moduleImplementation.name` if `name` is not provided so
   existing call sites still work unchanged.
3. Cast to `any` on the `new moduleImplementation()` call because TS
   narrows the constructor signature to `new () => InstanceType<...>`,
   which trips strict-mode TS in some downstream apps.

### Upstream status

- Tracked: search expo/expo issues for "registerWebModule minified class
  name" before removing — the upstream may have published a fix in 2.3+.
- Next time expo-modules-core is bumped: re-run `npx expo install` then
  diff `node_modules/expo-modules-core/src/registerWebModule.ts` against
  this patch. If upstream now passes a `name` argument, drop the patch.

### Owner

@MukundaKatta — bump-and-remove tracked in #196.

---

diff --git a/node_modules/expo-modules-core/src/registerWebModule.ts b/node_modules/expo-modules-core/src/registerWebModule.ts
index eaee38e..b02e459 100644
--- a/node_modules/expo-modules-core/src/registerWebModule.ts
+++ b/node_modules/expo-modules-core/src/registerWebModule.ts
@@ -10,10 +10,10 @@ import type { NativeModule } from './ts-declarations/NativeModule';
 export function registerWebModule<
   EventsMap extends Record<never, never>,
   ModuleType extends typeof NativeModule<EventsMap>,
->(moduleImplementation: ModuleType): ModuleType {
+>(moduleImplementation: ModuleType, name?: string): ModuleType {
   ensureNativeModulesAreInstalled();

-  const moduleName = moduleImplementation.name;
+  const moduleName = name || moduleImplementation.name;
   if (!moduleName) {
     throw new Error('Module implementation must be a class');
   }
@@ -23,6 +23,6 @@ export function registerWebModule<
   if (globalThis.expo.modules[moduleName]) {
     return globalThis.expo.modules[moduleName];
   }
-  globalThis.expo.modules[moduleName] = new moduleImplementation();
+  globalThis.expo.modules[moduleName] = new (moduleImplementation as any)();
   return globalThis.expo.modules[moduleName];
 }
